    "html": "\n      <p class=\"context\">Illustrative failures · two agents in one folder</p>\n      <h2>Separate chats still<br><em>share the machine.</em></h2>\n      <div class=\"collision-composition\">\n        <div class=\"collision-file\">\n          <span class=\"editorial-label\">Same file, different assumptions</span>\n          <div class=\"file-tab\"><span class=\"codicon codicon-file-code\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span> src/api.ts</div>\n          <div class=\"edit-fragment\"><span>Agent A</span><code>return { items, cursor };</code></div>\n          <div class=\"edit-fragment conflicting-edit arrival\" style=\"--delay:.7s\"><span>Agent B</span><code>return items;</code></div>\n          <p>One edit changes the code the other agent is using.</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"collision-terminal\">\n          <span class=\"editorial-label\">Different process, same port</span>\n          <div class=\"terminal-output\"><span class=\"terminal-actor\">Agent A</span><code>$ npm run dev</code><strong class=\"green\">Listening on :3000</strong><span class=\"terminal-actor\">Agent B</span><code>$ npm run dev</code><strong class=\"red arrival\" style=\"--delay:1s\">EADDRINUSE<br><small>address already in use :3000</small></strong></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"shared-pressure\"><span class=\"codicon codicon-server-process\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span><p>Builds, tests, and watchers also compete for <strong>CPU and memory.</strong></p></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"editorial-foot\"><span>Code conflicts and resource conflicts need different fixes.</span><span>Access to files, networks, and credentials is another boundary.</span></div>\n    ",
